> **SOKO** is proudly open-source under the MIT License. We believe in building together, transparency, and sharing knowledge. You are completely free to read, use, fork, and modify the code. Our core request is that you respect the work behind this project by **always giving proper credit to the original repository**.

<br>

## 📌 License summary

This is a quick guide to how you can use, modify, and share this project. *(Please note: This section is for informational purposes only and does not replace the official legal text below).*

### ✅ You are free to:
- **Use:** Download, compile, and use the software for personal, academic, or commercial purposes.
- **Modify:** Alter the source code to fit your specific needs or integrate it into your own systems.
- **Distribute & Fork:** Create your own versions, share them with the community, or fork the repository to build upon it.

### ⚠️ Under the following conditions:
- **Give Credit (Attribution):** If you fork this project, modify it, or use substantial portions of the code, you **must** provide a clear, visible link back to the official **[SOKO Repository](https://github.com/eldomiinus/soko)** in your `README.md` or documentation.
- **Keep Copyright Notices:** The original copyright notices and the permission notice must be included in all copies or substantial portions of the software.

### ❌ You cannot:
- **Hold us liable:** The software is provided "as is". The creators (Hoshi / eldomiinus) are not responsible for any damages, data loss, or issues arising from the use of this software.

